//===-- kernels.def - model-derived CUDA kernel variants ------*- C++ -*-===//
//
// Single source of truth for the kernel variants pie instantiates.
//
// Consumed twice, with no code generation step and no build-directory
// artifacts:
//   * C++   -- #include with the PIE_* macros defined; expands to explicit
//              instantiations, dispatch switch cases, constexpr tables and
//              #include lists.
//   * CMake -- file(STRINGS) + regex, to derive the per-head_dim translation
//              unit list and to decide whether the vendored FlashInfer fused
//              MoE launchers are reachable.
//
// ONLY model-derived axes belong here. The test is: can the value be decided
// from a checkpoint's config.json alone, without seeing a batch? If not, it
// is a runtime-policy axis and MUST stay fully instantiated -- pruning one
// turns a valid input into a runtime throw. Runtime-policy axes deliberately
// absent from this file:
//
//   attention  full_attention_variant (per batch, from num_requests),
//              CTA_TILE_Q (from plan_info), MaskMode (per call site),
//              logits_soft_cap
//   MoE        CUTLASS tile shape M/N/K and pipeline stages (occupancy
//              heuristic, resolved at run time)
//
// Target axes (sm80 vs sm90, CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES) stay in CMakeLists.txt.
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

#ifndef PIE_ATTN_HEAD_DIM
#define PIE_ATTN_HEAD_DIM(hd)
#endif
#ifndef PIE_ATTN_DECODE_GQA
#define PIE_ATTN_DECODE_GQA(g)
#endif
#ifndef PIE_MOE_ACTIVATION
#define PIE_MOE_ACTIVATION(name)
#endif

// ---- attention: head_dim --------------------------------------------------
// Checkpoint-derived, and pie accepts arbitrary HuggingFace repos
// (bin/pie/src/ops/model.rs maps model_type -> arch; it is not a list of known
// checkpoints). So this list stays PERMISSIVE: it is the set flashinfer
// supports, not the set we happen to have tested. Narrowing it would make an
// otherwise valid checkpoint fail at run time.
//
// The build win here is the translation-unit split, not pruning. cicc and
// ptxas are single-threaded per TU, so holding every head_dim in one file made
// it the build's critical path: 318s for the whole file versus 79s for
// head_dim=128 alone, against only ~5s of fixed per-TU overhead.
//
// config.cpp's round_up_head_dim() maps every checkpoint onto one of these
// four, so Phi-3-mini's 96 arrives as 128. 96 is deliberately absent: the
// prefill dispatch never had a 96 case, so a checkpoint that truly reached the
// kernels with 96 would already fail there -- which is what made the decode
// side's <96> instantiations detectable as dead.
PIE_ATTN_HEAD_DIM(64)   // llama3.2-1B
PIE_ATTN_HEAD_DIM(128)  // qwen3/qwen2/llama/mistral/olmo3, phi3 (96 -> 128)
PIE_ATTN_HEAD_DIM(256)  // gemma2/gemma3/gemma3n/gemma4 sliding layers
PIE_ATTN_HEAD_DIM(512)  // gemma4 global layers, deepseek_v2/v3/v4 MLA, kimi_k2

// ---- attention: decode GQA group size -------------------------------------
// num_q_heads / num_kv_heads. Tensor-parallel invariant: llama_like.cpp
// divides both by T, so the ratio is preserved. Must match flashinfer's
// DISPATCH_GQA_GROUP_SIZE set; ratios outside it (5/6/7) are routed to the
// prefill path by main.cpp's force_prefill_path gate and never reach decode.
PIE_ATTN_DECODE_GQA(1)
PIE_ATTN_DECODE_GQA(2)
PIE_ATTN_DECODE_GQA(3)
PIE_ATTN_DECODE_GQA(4)
PIE_ATTN_DECODE_GQA(8)

// ---- MoE: CUTLASS grouped-GEMM epilogue -----------------------------------
// FlashInfer's MoeGemmRunner::moeGemmBiasAct switches on a runtime
// ActivationType and instantiates one CUTLASS epilogue per case, dragging the
// whole grouped-GEMM template stack along with each. pie reaches exactly one:
// nemotron_h is the only consumer of CutlassMoeFCRunner and passes Relu2
// (ops/flashinfer_moe.cu holds the only ActivationType:: uses in
// crates/driver-cuda/csrc/src). pie's own code fixes this, not the checkpoint.
//
// Consequence for CMake: the vendored fused sm80 launchers are only reachable
// when the epilogue is Silu or FtGelu, so with Relu2 alone they are dead and
// third_party/flashinfer_generated/ drops out of the build entirely.
//
// NOTE: unlike attention, a missing entry here cannot be caught at
// compile time -- the arch -> runner binding is a runtime decision. Routing a
// new MoE arch through CutlassMoeFCRunner requires adding its activation here,
// or it throws at run time.
PIE_MOE_ACTIVATION(Relu2)     // nemotron_h
PIE_MOE_ACTIVATION(Swiglu)    // qwen3_5_moe fc1 (qwen3.5 / qwen3.6),
                              // glm5 / kimi / deepseek_v4 routed experts (fc1)
// Gemma-4 26B-A4B's routed experts. Upstream's `Geglu` IS the tanh
// approximation -- it dispatches to `EpilogueOpDefaultFtGelu`, the
// FasterTransformer GELU -- so it is the same function as pie's
// `launch_chunked_geglu_tanh_bf16`, not the erf form. `GegluTanh` is a
// separate upstream enumerator that `supportsFusedGatedActivation` does not
// accept, so routing Gemma-4 through it would silently lose the fused gate.
PIE_MOE_ACTIVATION(Geglu)     // gemma4 routed experts (fc1)
// A gated activation splits across the two grouped GEMMs: fc1 carries the
// gate (Swiglu above), and fc2's epilogue is plain Identity. Reaching one
// without the other throws at load time.
PIE_MOE_ACTIVATION(Identity)  // second grouped GEMM (fc2) of every gated MoE

// ---- all-reduce: fused residual+RMSNorm epilogue --- RETIRED --------------
// This axis had exactly one consumer, `comm/custom_all_reduce.cu`, and that
// file is DELETED. The axis is gone with it; nothing in CMake ever read it
// (`pie_read_def_list` is called for PIE_ATTN_HEAD_DIM only), so removing it
// reconciles nothing.
//
// The ARGUMENT it made is not retired, and it is now
// `driver-cuda/src/fire/all_reduce.rs`, in Rust, as constants a test checks.
// It read:
//
//   flashinfer's allreduce_fusion_op() turns four runtime values into one
//   compile-time cross product:
//
//     switch (nranks) {2,4,8,16} x switch (pattern) {10} x fp32_acc {2}
//       x (oneshot x trigger_completion_at_end {2}, or twoshot {1})
//
//   which is 240 kernels -- 96% of every kernel in custom_all_reduce.cu, and
//   the reason that translation unit cost 111s (40s cicc + 44s ptxas).
//
//   pie reaches exactly one pattern: kARResidualRMSNorm. The other nine are
//   FP8/FP4 quant epilogues that no pie call site can select.
//
//   allreduce_fusion_kernel_launcher is public, so custom_all_reduce.cu
//   expanded this list into its own dispatch switch and never called
//   flashinfer's. That also meant a missing entry surfaced as a RUNTIME
//   THROW, not a link error.
//
//   nranks stayed hand-written and fully instantiated: TP world size is a
//   deployment choice, not a checkpoint property, and {2,4,8,16} is
//   upstream's supported set rather than a pie-owned axis.
//
// Three of those sentences change meaning on the other side and are restated
// there rather than copied:
//
//  * `INSTANTIATED` is the one pattern, `NRANKS` is upstream's set, and
//    `AOT_POINTS_AFTER_PRUNING` is the 24 this pruning actually built.
//  * The 111s was an argument about an AHEAD-OF-TIME translation unit. Under
//    NVRTC the unit of work is one instantiation, ~0.46s, compiled on first
//    call and cached; the list stops being "which were BUILT" and becomes
//    "which are REACHABLE", which is checkable before a fire instead of
//    during one.
//  * "A missing entry surfaces as a runtime throw" is the failure shape this
//    migration converts. It is a `Decline::PatternNotInstantiated` now, and
//    `#[must_use] enum AllReduce { Launched, Declined(_) }` is what stops it
//    being spelled like a success.
